+# MedSafe
+
+Medication-safety decision-support research prototype. It demonstrates conservative prescription parsing, source-tracked rules, and an API. **Research prototype, not for clinical use.**
+
+## What it does
+
+The project parses a narrow set of prescription directions, normalizes documented drug names, and reports findings from local rules. A local model can add explicitly unverified estimates for some DDInter-listed pairs whose source severity is unspecified. Findings retain their source evidence, and unresolved input stays visible.
+
+The rule engine loads 313 DDInter DDI rules for a whitelist of 30 drugs. These are a subset of the DDInter dataset, not its complete collection. Some source severities are unspecified; their findings require pharmacist review. Mechanisms and recommendations remain empty when the source dataset does not provide them.
+
+## Data sources and attribution
+
+DDI rules derive from DDInter, Computational Biology & Drug Design Group ([download](https://ddinter.scbdd.com/download/), [terms](https://ddinter.scbdd.com/terms/)). The source dataset is licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Review the source terms before redistribution or commercial use. See [data/raw/ddinter/SOURCE.md](data/raw/ddinter/SOURCE.md) and [reports/ddinter_import.md](reports/ddinter_import.md). Imported derivative rows retain the applicable attribution and license information.
+
+Drug-class lookup uses the NLM RxClass API. NLM attribution: “This product uses publicly available data from the U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM), National Institutes of Health, Department of Health and Human Services; NLM is not responsible for the product and does not endorse or recommend this or any other product.”
+
+Allergy and drug-disease rows cite DailyMed labels in their source fields. No dose rows are currently loaded.
+
+## Install
+
+Requires Python 3.11 or newer.
+
+```powershell
+python -m venv .venv
+.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
+pip install -e ".[dev,ml]"
 ```
-Imported DDInter rules load from `data/seed/rules.csv`. Name synonyms load from `data/seed/synonyms.csv`. Exact verified mappings resolve automatically. RapidFuzz scores >=95 auto-accept; 90 to <95 return a suggestion and require confirmation; lower scores stay unresolved. Bare Crocin, Dolo, and Brufen product-family names stay unresolved. `Dolo 650` and `Crocin Advance 500mg` resolve; `Crocin 500mg` stays unresolved because that shorthand omits the verified product variant. Combination synonyms return every verified ingredient. The current analysis engine does not expand multi-ingredient results into separate DDI checks, so it marks those prescriptions unresolved rather than claiming a clear result.
-The graph loader reads drug classes only from `data/seed/drug_classes.csv`; class rules load from `data/seed/class_rules.csv`. Exact-name ATC matches were retrieved from NLM RxClass. Three names remain `TODO_VERIFY`; no class was guessed. See `reports/drug_class_verification.json`. Graph class matching is infrastructure only; no clinical class rule is currently populated. Export MAJOR rows for manual review with `python scripts/export_review_sheet.py`; apply only complete source-backed reviews with `python scripts/apply_review.py`. No rule is marked reviewed until reviewer, date, and source are present.
-Import DDInter data after placing its original files in `data/raw/ddinter/` with `python scripts/import_ddinter.py`. The checked-in subset is already imported from the source files and whitelist. Review status is explicit; `reviewed_by` and `verified_on` remain blank until a human performs review.
-Current import audit is saved in `data/seed/ddinter_import_report.json` and `reports/ddinter_import.md`. It records source label counts, preserved unspecified rows, unmapped labels, duplicate conflicts, and whitelist coverage. `data/review/major_rules_review.csv` contains all 21 MAJOR rows, ready for manual source review.
-## Current limits
-- Small exact alias list; no RxNorm service integration or fuzzy auto-selection.
-- Parser supports a narrow `drug dose unit frequency` format.
-- No clinical DDI, drug-disease, cross-reactivity, or dose thresholds loaded.
-- No PHI storage, authentication, audit service, FHIR integration, or clinical validation.
-- No LLM. Future use must remain limited to parsing or wording and must not change findings.
 
